# Engineering standards (authoritative)

Base every decision on **[docs/AGENT-PLAYBOOK.md](../../docs/AGENT-PLAYBOOK.md)** —
read it before non-trivial work. It governs the 3D/asset pipeline, bundle
budget, performance, UX/motion, git, security, the non-engineer content
workflow (§11), the plan-first working method (§12), deployment readiness
(§13), and the UX "feel" toolbox (§14). Worked examples of the method are in
`docs/plans/`. If a request conflicts with the playbook, follow the playbook
and say so.

## Hard rules (do not violate without the user's explicit, in-context approval)

- **Definition of Done.** Never call work complete, commit, or push until all
  four gates pass: `npx tsc -b`, `npx vite build`, `npm run check:bundle`,
  `npm run test:visual`. A red gate is a blocker — report it, don't push.
- **Red-zone files need approval first.** Do NOT edit without asking:
  `src/components/three/**`, `src/three/**`, `scripts/**`, any `*.glb` /
  `public/models/**`, `src/components/three/sceneConfig.ts`, `vite.config.ts`,
  `tsconfig*.json`, `package.json`, lockfiles, `check-bundle.mjs`. If a task
  seems to need one, stop and explain why before touching it.
- **Content in data files, not components.** Copy/specs/image lists live in
  typed data modules (`websiteData.ts`, `websiteRootsData.ts`, `src/data/*`).
- **Images:** after replacing any raster in `public/`, regenerate its
  `.avif`/`.webp` siblings (`npm run compress:images`) — the browser serves
  the old art otherwise. Diagnose blank/mismatched assets with `file`.
- **Colors:** only via existing design tokens (`--warm-*`, `--web-*`); never
  hardcode brand hex. See `design-system.mdc`.
- **Scope discipline.** Keep a change to one concern and the fewest files. A
  copy/image edit that touches engine or build files is wrong — re-scope it.
- **Git:** work on a branch, never edit `main` directly; never rewrite pushed
  history; commit messages state the *why* (with numbers for tuning changes).
- **Verify visual changes** with screenshots; refresh visual-test baselines
  only after reading the diffs, and commit them with the change.
- **Plan non-trivial work in review-gated phases** (§12): diagnose root cause
  first, land foundation/perf before polish, state what's out of scope, and
  **flag any change to the visual design for approval before making it** — the
  designer keeps creative control; you keep the discipline.
- **Deployment:** don't call anything production-ready until the §13 checklist
  passes (SPA rewrites, no preview-only URLs, graceful fallbacks, meta/OG,
  asset diet, every route 404-free in `vite preview`).

## When unsure

Prefer the conservative path in the playbook, reuse existing
components/tokens over new dependencies, and ask the user rather than edit a
red-zone file or push a red gate.
